    <string name="_ms_fansonly_help_text"><![CDATA[
<p> </p>
<p><strong>General Settings</strong></p>
<ul>
    <li>Enable option on Module</li>
</ul>

<p style="padding-left: 30px;">Select from this list of forms, in which one of them the switch "This content is for my fans only" will be displayed.</p>
   
<p> </p>

<ul>
    <li>Replacement Image in Content Page</li>
</ul>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;">Upload a custom image to replace the content's header image or preview photo in listings (Grids) and Conten's page. Image recommended size: 1280x720 pixels. Image must be in a widescreen aspect ratio 16:9. If your image contains text, the text must be centered so it can be read in all screen sizes.</p>


<p> </p>

<ul>
    <li>Replacement Image in Forum Grid Mini Description</li>
</ul>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;">Upload a custom mini image to replace the Discussion's Text in the Grids listings.( Eg. domain.com/page/discussions-home ). </p>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;"> This photo will replace the Discussion preview text in the grids, recommended size is: 200x27 pixels.
</p>


<p> </p>
<ul>
    <li>Enable Free Requests</li>
</ul>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;">Check this option if you want to enable free requests</p>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;"> If this is enabled, users will be able to request free access to private content. Content owner can accept or ignore the request. If a request is accepted by a content owner, all private content from him/her will be available for the requester. There is no payment involved and there is no expiration date, content owner can remove free access to users previously accepted anytime.</p>


<p> </p>

<ul>
    <li>Disable paid buttons</li>
</ul>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;">Check this option if you want to remove paid Subscription buttons for everyone</p>
<p style="padding-left: 30px;">This is useful if you need free requests only and don't need them to pay to watch private content. If you need to give users the hability to earn money, do not enable this.
</p>


]]></string>
    
    
